{"chunk_id": "22fb9d712aed", "text": "This section recounts the aftermath of a secret plot by Duryodhana, Karna, Sakuni, and Duhsasana\u2014approved by Dhritarashtra\u2014to burn Kunti and the five Pandavas alive in the flammable house at Varanavata. Vidura, perceptive and loyal to the Pandavas, discerns the conspiracy and secretly arranges their escape by boat across the Ganges. The Pandavas flee into the forest while the lac house burns, killing the architect Purochana and an unfortunate Nishada woman with her children, leading the public to believe the Pandavas have died. Dhritarashtra and the Kuru court perform false mourning rites. The narrative then reveals Duryodhana\u2019s deeper motive: jealousy of Bhima\u2019s strength, Arjuna\u2019s prowess, and especially the growing public support for Yudhishthira as rightful king, which threatens the Kauravas\u2019 claim to the throne.\nDuryodhana conspires to burn the Pandavas in the lac house, but Vidura secretly helps Kunti and her sons escape across the Ganges.\nThemes: court intrigue, jealousy and succession, secret rescue, deception, family rivalry", "vector": [0.00035424300585873425, -0.008096982724964619, -0.003570977132767439, -0.0013270055642351508, -0.021591953933238983, 0.020443152636289597, -0.019391236826777458, -0.003024257719516754, -0.013633381575345993, -0.012228520587086678, 0.017135154455900192, 0.012193918228149414, 0.015377347357571125, 0.02058156207203865, -0.012041667476296425, 0.007827083580195904, 0.0330246165394783, -0.013328880071640015, 0.04420814290642738, -0.029453640803694725, -0.016789129003882408, -0.007667912170290947, -0.006027753930538893, 0.030173372477293015, -0.019183620810508728, 0.018685344606637955, 0.0038893199525773525, -0.01761958934366703, 0.01042919047176838, -0.00024286624102387577, 0.0018616140587255359, -0.006875514984130859, 0.016802970319986343, -0.014685297384858131, -0.02181341126561165, 0.01401400938630104, -0.013363482430577278, -0.019488122314214706, 0.005380687